From dfb20b706b8471fd421c92048300c14c6cdfee5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 13:36:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XD Netplay: host trainer name in the room, silent battle
 music, raise-to-100 opt-in, GBA link progress OSD (v1.5.8)

- Host can set its in-game trainer name from the netplay room on desktop
  and Android (RenameHostTrainer: GBA port 2 save, OT re-stamp, verified
  write); the bundled templates ship as Player1/Player2 and the team
  editor's field was the only place to change it.
- Battle music gains 'No music (silent battle)': writes 0 into the VS BGM
  table, the engine's own start-nothing sentinel (id==0 skip in the
  streamed-voice starter); SFX untouched. Table id 0x10000 so it can never
  collide with 'Game default'.
- Raise to Lv. 100, opt-in only: team editor button (level-100 formats
  only) and a Submit Team checkbox carried as a RaiseLevel100 header,
  applied by the host only under a level-100 format. Only ever raises.
- On-screen progress for the fixed GBA link ladder (negotiating / upload
  percent / client starting), counted per lock so rematches read right.
- First-screen copy states host-only picks vs what a joiner sets in the
  next window; hint copy for the host name field.
